//! `@std/ui` — one library for every surface. A view is a function of
//! state that answers COMPONENTS; a component projects to a neutral
//! `Node`; a target draws the tree and reports what the user did; `mount`
//! runs the loop. docs/2026_10_05_UI_ARCHITECTURE.md is the law.
//!
//!     use @std.ui.components.{column, text, button}
//!     use @std.ui.web.{mount}
//!
//!     state count: int = 0
//!
//!     fn view() -> column {
//!         column {
//!             text "${count} presses"
//!             button "Count" { on press { count = count + 1 } }
//!         }
//!     }
//!
//!     mount(view)
//!
//! | module | holds |
//! |---|---|
//! | `components` | the controls and containers a view is written in |
//! | `style` | `Style`, `Layout`, `Theme` and the tokens they name |
//! | `realize` | `View`, `Node`, and each target's drawing of a tree |
//! | `web` | `mount` on a page |
//! | `terminal` | `mount` in a terminal |
//! | `headless` | a screen held in memory, for tests |
